This repository distributes a Derivative Work of the WaLa code base
(https://github.com/AutodeskAILab/WaLa). As required by Section 4.1 of that licence,
the Materials have been changed, and the changes are the following.

Changes to the model code in src/, relative to the public WaLa repository:

  1. Apple Silicon support: the model runs on the Metal (MPS) backend. This required
     converting float64 tensors to float32 at several points, a native build path for
     the sparse-convolution dependency, and small JSON fixes in the shipped configs.

  2. Memory: gradient checkpointing on the diffusion transformer, which lowers the
     peak memory of a backward pass through the model from about 21 GB to about 6.5 GB
     and makes gradient-based guidance feasible on a laptop-class GPU.

  3. A learned fusion module, added for the paper's negative baseline (Section VI-E):
     a cross-attention block with an exact pass-through at initialisation, and geometry
     encoders for voxel and point-cloud inputs, trained on top of the frozen model. It
     is off by default and is not used by the anchoring method.

  4. Three upstream pull requests of the public repository merged in: additional
     conditioning modalities, a norm-layer argument on DiT blocks for timm
     compatibility, and the optimised-inference path.

The constraint-anchoring method itself (tools/guided_sampling.py) does not modify the
model or its weights. It wraps the denoising network at sampling time and corrects its
prediction with the gradient of a geometric residual.

Model weights are not distributed here. They are fetched from the Hugging Face hub
under their own licence.
